#op: develop
A field both versions declare, and no lens mentions, is copied. The copy has
to produce a value the target accepts. Here kind narrows from any string to
two of them, and the ForwardLens does not map it.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	name: string
	kind: string
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	name: string
	kind: "a" | "b"
}

ForwardLens: {
	v0_0: _
	tip: {
		name: v0_0.name
	}
}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0358",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "the ForwardLens of tip would copy v0_0.kind into kind, which does not accept every value of it",
      "primary": {
        "file": "tip.thema",
        "line": 6,
        "col": 1,
        "offset": 44,
        "origin": "user"
      },
      "notes": [
        {
          "label": "both v0.0 and tip declare kind, so a lens that does not map it copies it"
        },
        {
          "label": "kind in tip is now \"a\" | \"b\", which does not accept every value of the prior string"
        }
      ],
      "help": [
        "map kind in the ForwardLens: a _match, a computed value, or a constant"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "errors": 1,
    "warnings": 0,
    "notes": 0
  }
}
